fied predicate.\r\n\r\n```gd\r\nvar array: Array[int] = [ 0, 1, 2, 3, 10 ]\r\nvar remove_count: int = array.erase_custom(func(v: int): return v % 2 == 0)\r\nprint(remove_count, \" \", array) # Prints 3 [1, 3]\r\n```\r\n\r\n<hr>\r\n\r\nCurrently I don't think there is a good way to remove elements from an Array in a loop. You can either remove by iterating from the end ...\r\n```gd\r\nvar array: Array[int] = [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5]\r\nfor i in range(array.size()-1, -1, -1):\r\n\tarray.remove_at(i)\r\n```\r\n... or just design around the idea, that you'll not be able to do so.","labels":[{"id":73330068,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2OA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/feature%20proposal","name":"feature proposal","description":"","color":"4466ff","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279096997,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTY5OTc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/archived","name":"archived","description":"","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279097966,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTc5NjY=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:core","name":"topic:core","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2025-02-16T09:47:16Z","updated_at":"2025-02-17T18:25:39Z","closed_at":"2025-02-16T17:22:03Z","merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"aa2d775a36a4947e6c283b070ea541ee23a166cb","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"A-Machynak:array_erase_custom","ref":"array_erase_custom","repo":null,"sha":"8d4e90c4a49556e36a66812cd0bac405fcfc5560","user":{"login":"A-Machynak","id":99248176,"node_id":"U_kgDOBepoMA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99248176?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/A-Machynak","html_url":"https://github.com/A-Machynak","followers_